# S10.2D-R1 Community preflight command diagnosis — 2026-09-05

## Safe result

The read-only BotFather capability check completed green. The following
temporary target-archive verification stopped before provider verification
because the manually composed archive extraction command named a nonexistent
executable. `set -e` stopped immediately and the exact `mktemp` directory had
an EXIT cleanup trap. No repository, configuration, service, database,
Telegram or public state was changed.

## Root cause and bounded correction

This was a command transcription error, not a product or infrastructure
failure. The correction is to reuse the already reviewed sequence from
`target_community_verify`: create one exact `/run` scratch directory, stream
the exact target Git archive into standard `tar -x -C`, execute the official
read-only Community verifier, and delete only that scratch directory through
the existing `find "$scratch" -depth -delete` pattern.

No deployment, retry or new architecture is authorized by this diagnosis.

## Fresh-backup wrapper diagnosis

The versioned backup creator completed and its own checks reported both Git
bundles valid. A separately composed wrapper then exited non-zero because it
looked for `manifest.sha256`; the versioned backup format uses `SHA256SUMS`.
No deployment or runtime change had started.

Two subsequent read-only verification attempts also stopped without mutation:
the first invoked `git bundle verify` without a repository, and the second used
the wrong Application repository path and a user that cannot traverse the
root-owned backup directory. The bounded final verification used the actual
Application repository `/opt/tu1nz_repos/adult-publishing-core`, explicit Git
safe-directory declarations, and root read access only. `SHA256SUMS` verified,
both bundles verified, the backup remained root-owned with mode `2700`, and all
30 expected top-level evidence files were present.

The accepted fresh pre-cutover backup is:
`/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s8-public-telegram/20260905T120531Z-pre-s10-2d-r1-community`.
No second backup or deployment retry was started.

## Controller backup-path boundary stop

After this diagnosis was integrated, the Control commit changed, so the
controller correctly required a newly bound backup. That backup verified
successfully but was named with the suffix `-pre-s10-2d-r1-final`. The
versioned controller accepts only paths ending exactly in
`-pre-s10-2d-community`; its read-only preflight therefore stopped with
`BACKUP_PATH_OUTSIDE_BOUNDARY` before any quiesce, migration, deployment or
runtime mutation.

The bounded correction is documentation-first integration of this stop,
followed by Control synchronization and one new backup created with the exact
versioned suffix. The earlier backups remain immutable evidence; no deployment
attempt or rollback has occurred.

## Single cutover failure and fail-closed recovery — 2026-09-05

The subsequent exact-path preflight passed. The single authorized deployment
attempt switched to the bound target but failed during the publication-rotation
health sequence after the local S8 endpoint on port 18110 was unavailable and
the rotation service exited non-zero. The controller immediately invoked its
versioned rollback. It restored the Application repository to the source commit,
restored the database without migration 0029, and restored the source files.

The rollback then stopped before restarting public services and timers because
the current public bot still had BotFather group membership enabled. The source
contract requires it disabled, and Telegram does not expose this capability as
an ordinary bot-API mutation. The controller therefore returned
`SOURCE_BOTFATHER_GROUPS_OPERATOR_REQUIRED` and left the public S8/S10 services
and S9/S10 timers inactive, while S7 and nginx remained active. Public WMS
returned 502; the legacy redirect remained 308. Both repositories were clean,
Application was back at the source commit, and migration 0029 was absent.

### Approved recovery plan

1. The operator sets BotFather Join Groups to Disabled for `@wantmeseenbot`.
2. Run the existing versioned `rollback` action with Control commit
   `8f4dc153a8d9a6997e7c63a3aecff6504c8d3588`, tree
   `07e52e069d7fe4023c7bb38f495ae3624e8e1cc0`, and the exact pre-cutover backup
   `/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s8-public-telegram/20260905T121330Z-pre-s10-2d-community`.
3. Verify source Application/Control provenance, migration absence, all source
   services and timers, public 200/308 endpoints, zero restarts, and closed Adult
   boundaries read-only.
4. Do not attempt S10.2D deployment again. Keep real acquisition NO-GO and
   version this diagnosis only after the safe source state is restored.
